00:00:01.699 --> 00:00:03.409 align:start position:0%
teaching from mastery learning means  that teachers only move on to the next  subject once everyone has mastered a  current unit in other words there's no  good enough only perfect traditionally  we set a fixed amount of time to study a  unit and allow for flexible outcomes for  example one year of basic algebra  returns students with grades from A to F  teaching for mastery turns this around  all students attain an a even if it  requires more than a year for example a  math teacher ensures that everybody  knows how to compute addition before  going on to more difficult units such as  multiplication or division this prevents  growing knowledge gaps and increases  unity among classmates with no one left  behind teaching for mastery demands  perfection if you asked at what  temperature does water start boiling  don't accept 100 dig deeper until the  student replies that the boiling point  of water depends on the atmospheric  pressure which changes according to  elevation at sea level it is 100 degrees  Celsius but it boils at a lower  temperature in higher altitudes teaching  for mastery requires clear learning  goals detailed tracking students  progress and diverse opportunities to  catch up for those who fall behind some  schools even reorganize classes by the  students level of understanding instead  of age if you are interested to learn  more about this method please check out  the links in the description and let us  know in the comments how you can see it  applied in class the Khan Academy orgy  features great examples on how to set  clear learning goals with its knowledge  map and study videos for students who  need to catch up or releasing videos  regularly so don't forget to subscribe  and like us on Facebook thank you for  watching
 

